      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2008-p24.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(\\frac{-1}{2007}\\) Notice that, if \\(x \\neq 0,1\\), then \\(f^{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{1-x}}=\\frac{x-1}{x}\\), which means that \\(f^{3}(x)=\\) \\(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{x-1}{x}}=x\\). So \\(f^{n}\\) is periodic with period \\(n=3\\), which means that \\(f^{2007}(x)=x\\) so \\(f^{2008}(2008)=\\) \\(f(2008)=\\frac{-1}{2007}\\).\n\\(1^{\\text {st }}\\) HARVARD-MIT NOVEMBER TOURNAMENT, 8 SATURDAY 2008 - GUTS ROUND",
